# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client environment. Next.js reads env from THIS directory, not the repo root,
# so anything the browser needs goes here rather than in the root `.env`.
#
# This file is gitignored (via `*.local`). Copy to `.env.local` and edit that.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Development sign-in shortcuts -----------------------------------------
# Adds a row of "fill the form as a role" buttons to /login.
#
# The buttons appear ONLY when this is exactly "1". The seed already refuses to
# create demo accounts when NODE_ENV=production; this is the second lock on the
# same door. Never enable it on a shared or reachable deployment.
#
# Filling the email needs no secret, so it works as soon as the flag is set.
# Filling the password is opt-in: a NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is inlined into the client
# bundle at build time, and there is no way to autofill a password from the
# browser without putting it there. Leave the two passwords blank and the buttons
# fill the email only, which is the safe default.
#
# The password here must match SEED_DEMO_PASSWORD in the repo root .env, which is
# the value the API actually authenticates against. They live in different files
# because the two processes read different directories - rotate both, and a stale
# value here fails the sign-in loudly rather than granting anything wrong.
#
# Quote any value containing '#' or a space: an unquoted '#' starts a comment and
# silently truncates the value.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_LOGIN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_PASSWORD=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_ADMIN_PASSWORD=""

# --- Direct API access (optional) ------------------------------------------
# Leave unset to use the Next.js proxy on /api/*, which keeps the session cookie
# first-party and avoids CORS. Set only for deliberate cross-origin calls; the
# API must then allow this origin via CLIENT_ORIGIN.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000